WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.300
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.600
So I’ve been told three times in the last week
by creative people running cool businesses

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.200
that they “really respect my business skills,”
and to that, I just would like to say…

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.760
[LAUGHS]

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.280
The list of my screw-ups is a mile long
and full of cringe.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.300
Now I’m not saying that I’m not
interested in it, haven’t worked hard.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.000
There are reasons why I’m fairly good at this.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.700
A big one is that I do like solving problems,
I like getting a good feel for them

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.640
and finding different ways to attack them
and worrying about them.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.650
I find this to be fun, creative work that’s
actually kind of similar to plotting a novel?

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.740
Two, I see it as good.
Employing people, treating them fairly,

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.859
creating value for the world,
finding ways for that value to sustain itself.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:43.000
Three, my dad has run businesses, and whenever
I have a problem I can call him and he helps me.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.859
It’s… extremely valuable!

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.500
I could go on!
Four, I’ve gotten very lucky with hiring.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.980
And all those things have helped, and I’m
happy to take some credit where it’s due,

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.800
but ultimately I have a secret.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:01:01.640
And it will be absolutely no help when I tell you about it.
Every business I have launched that has succeeded

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:06.250
has been launched with the support
of a really wonderful online community.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.260
Honestly, this is part of why DFTBA now gives
all of John and my profit

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.160
to the Maternal Center of Excellence
in Sierra Leone.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.780
It’s why the Vlogbrothers channel revenue
has always been split

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.440
between charity and supporting
smaller educational video channels.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.720
When I look at this honestly and objectively
and I think about where the value came from,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.820
it always feels to me like a lot of the value
came from the employees and this community

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.520
and less from me,
because I’m just one person, right?

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.060
There are times when I have pounded myself
into the ground to get things done.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.240
I’ve had a lot of bad weeks in my life.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.770
But in running a business, it’s important
to understand where your value comes from.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.860
It’s important to understand your strengths.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.760
And this community has always been at the
top of the list of our strengths.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:53.700
And that’s not just like marketing to you.
It’s finding people who can tell us

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.340
how to do things, finding people to hire.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.710
Getting immediate product feedback! Like there’s
a reason I keep talking about soda syrups.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.820
I’m trying to get you guys to tell me how
you feel about soda syrups!

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:07.980
And basically no one has this asset.
Now, other people have similar assets,

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.590
but not like Nerdfighteria, right?
Not this good!

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:14.740
So I’ve been hesitant to give advice when my biggest
asset is something that I don’t tend to share… but!

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:19.060
I would like... for us... to build a business!
Now here’s how it’s gonna work.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.620
If you are a business person and you think
you could help this idea by

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.990
providing mentorship or helping us pick business
ideas that are submitted to us,

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.099
I’ve created a form in the description,
and it’s next to the words, “I can help.”

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:34.269
If you think you have expertise that will
be valuable on a small board of people

00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:37.420
making decisions and providing mentorship,
fill that out!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.920
Second, if you are an entrepreneur, if you have a
product or a service that you are excited about

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.120
that you’ve started to grow
but you need a push,

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.939
I’ve got a form for you as well.
It’s called, “I need help.”

00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:50.660
Now in general, we’re looking for stuff
that’s beyond the idea stage

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.409
and that it actually has a product or service
or business developed a little bit.

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:59.519
You can fill this out with just an idea, but...
it better be a banger, basically.

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:03.959
But here’s the sticky bit:
I’m gonna give this business $50,000… but!

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:07.680
If the business is able to become successful
over the next three years,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.510
we wanna get that $50,000 back
to promote maternal health in Sierra Leone.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.260
And every year when you do your profit distributions,
10% of after-tax income

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.620
should also go to support that effort.

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:23.209
If that sounds good to you and you’ve got
an idea that can grow but needs some mentorship

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:27.860
and some support from an amazing audience
of cool people who wanna support good things,

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.560
the form is down in the description.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:35.160
John, I think everybody has the ability to be a
business owner. Now, not everybody has the inclination.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.599
But even if you don’t,
I think everyone should watch

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:39.450
the Crash Course Business: Entrepreneurship
Learning Playlist.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.840
It’s a 17-episode series hosted by Anna Akana
that goes over the basics

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.150
of starting your own business
and also of business in general.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.180
The link to that playlist is here
and in the description,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.859
and those forms that I was telling you about
are down there as well.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.440
John, I’ll see you on Tuesday.

